---
description: Express layers, auth, and error conventions under src/
globs: src/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# src/

- Routes wire middlewares and controllers. Controllers call services. Services talk to models. Do not query Mongoose from a route file.
- Wrap controller handlers with `asyncWrapper`. Do not leave unhandled promise rejections in routes.
- Throw `src/utils/errorsHelper.js`. The error middleware returns JSON `{ status, code, message }`.
- Auth: Bearer access token via `authMiddleware`. Roles via `restrictTo(...)`. Refresh token is an httpOnly cookie.
- Request bodies: `validationMiddleware` + schemas in `src/validation/schemas/`.
- Mail language: `langMiddleware` (`en` / `ua`) and Pug under `src/emails/`.
- Env-backed values live in `src/configs/config.js`. Do not read `process.env` in controllers.
